---
import Company from '../layouts/Company.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.js';
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---
<Company title="Terms of Sale & Refunds — Asking Company" description="Terms of sale, refund policy and privacy notice for Asking Company. What you buy, what it costs, how refunds work, and what we store." page="legal">

  <div class="note" style="--corner:'§'">
    <span class="corner tr">&sect;</span><span class="corner bl">&sect;</span>
    <span class="eyebrow">Terms of Sale</span>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(32px,6.4vw,54px)">Terms of Sale<br>&amp; Refunds.</h2>
    <p class="dim">The rest of this website is a joke. This page is not. It sets out plainly
      what you are paying for, how to get your money back, and what we keep.</p>
    <p class="tiny" style="margin-top:18px">Last updated 1 October 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="terms">

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">1 &middot; Who we are</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>This website is operated by <b>Asking Company</b>, based in {SITE.city}.
          In these terms, "we", "us" and "our" mean Asking Company, and "you" means the person
          making a payment.</p>
        <p>You can contact us at any time by email: <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">2 &middot; What you are buying</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>When you make a payment on this website you are buying one <b>Certificate of
          Nothing</b>: a digital certificate recording your payment, the amount paid, and your
          giver number (your position in the sequence of everyone who has paid).</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The certificate is delivered <b>immediately on screen</b> once your payment is
            complete, and you can download it as an image file.</li>
          <li>Nothing physical is shipped. No further goods, services, rights or benefits are
            provided or promised.</li>
          <li>The certificate is a novelty item. It does not represent ownership of anything.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">3 &middot; Price and payment</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul>
          <li>Prices start from <b>US$1</b>. The exact amount is always shown to you
            <b>before</b> you pay.</li>
          <li>You may choose to pay more than US$1 by accepting the optional prompts that offer
            to double the amount. You are never required to pay more than the amount you
            confirm.</li>
          <li>Payments are processed by <b>Stripe</b>. Your card details are entered into
            Stripe's secure payment form and are handled by Stripe, not by us. <b>We do not see
            or store your card details.</b></li>
          <li>Each payment is a single, one-time charge. There are no subscriptions and no
            recurring charges.</li>
          <li>Your bank or card issuer may charge its own fees (for example, currency conversion
            fees). Those are outside our control.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">4 &middot; Refunds</span>
      <div class="panel spot">
        <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:14px"><b>If you want your money back, you can have it.</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a> within <b>30 days</b> of your payment.</li>
          <li>Include your receipt (or the email address you paid with, the date and the
            amount) so we can find the payment.</li>
          <li>We will refund the <b>full amount</b> to your original payment method.
            <b>No questions asked.</b></li>
          <li>Refunds are issued through Stripe. They usually appear on your statement within
            5&ndash;10 business days, depending on your bank.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:14px">If something has gone wrong with a payment &mdash;
          a duplicate charge, an amount you did not intend, or a charge you do not recognise
          &mdash; please email us first. We will sort it out.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">5 &middot; The public ledger</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul>
          <li>After paying you may choose to add a name to the public ledger on the home page.
            This is <b>optional</b>. If you leave it blank, no name is shown.</li>
          <li>The name you choose must not be offensive and must not impersonate another person
            or organisation.</li>
          <li>We may edit or remove any name from the public ledger at our discretion, at any
            time, without notice. Removing a name does not affect your payment or your
            certificate.</li>
          <li>If you would like your name removed, email us and we will remove it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">6 &middot; Privacy</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>For each payment we store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>the name you chose for the ledger, if any;</li>
          <li>the amount paid;</li>
          <li>the date of payment; and</li>
          <li>Stripe's payment reference, so that we can find the payment for refunds and
            enquiries.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Stripe processes your payment details (including your card and email address) under
          its own privacy policy.</p>
        <p>We only send you emails if you choose to subscribe to them, and you can unsubscribe
          at any time. <b>We do not sell or rent your data</b> to anyone.</p>
        <p>To ask what we hold about you, or to have it deleted (subject to any records we are
          legally required to keep), email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">7 &middot; What this is not</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>A payment on this website is a purchase of a novelty digital certificate and
          nothing else. It is <b>not</b>:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>a security, share, equity, token or ownership interest of any kind;</li>
          <li>an investment or a loan, and it carries no expectation of any return; or</li>
          <li>a donation to a registered charity, and it is not tax deductible.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Asking Company is a satirical project. The company figures, staff, corporate
          structure and other material elsewhere on this site are written as satire. See the
          <a href="#disclaimer">satire disclaimer</a> below.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <span class="eyebrow">8 &middot; Governing law</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws
          of Canada applicable there. Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have under
          consumer protection law that cannot be excluded by agreement.</p>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version in force when you make a
          payment applies to that payment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk" id="disclaimer">
      <span class="eyebrow">Satire disclaimer</span>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="dim">Asking Company is a satirical project. Nothing on this site is an offer to
          sell or a solicitation of an offer to buy any security, and no security, equity, share,
          unit, token, or ownership interest of any kind exists or is contemplated. Financial
          figures quoted elsewhere on the site are real but trivial; forward-looking statements
          are almost certainly false. Persons named as employees do not work here and have not
          been contacted. None of this affects your rights under these terms: the price, the
          certificate, the refund policy and the privacy commitments above are meant exactly
          as written.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <div class="panel narrow" style="text-align:center">
        <p><b>Questions about any of this?</b></p>
        <p class="dim" style="font-size:15px">Email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>. A real
          person reads it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</Company>

<style is:global>
  .terms .panel{font-size:16px;line-height:1.65}
  .terms .panel ul{margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:22px}
  .terms .panel ul:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .terms .panel li{margin-bottom:8px}
</style>
